A certificate was issued to log in as you at a console -- a physical
terminal, a serial console, or a BMC viewer on the machine below.

If you just typed a code from that screen into the web UI and approved the
login, this is it and there is nothing to do.

If you did not, someone got a console login in your name approved. That takes
your web session, so treat it as a compromised session: sign out everywhere,
change whatever protects your identity provider account, then tell whoever
runs that machine. The certificate below is live until it expires and cannot
be recalled.

